    "content": "\"For each item below, fetch its source and check that the recorded quote appears on the page and supports the item. A card item is a field of the plan in the producer's words, with the sources it cites: check each factual claim in it against those sources, and any value it carries against the page; what the plan will build, measure or predict needs no source, but a factual claim with no source is UNSUPPORTED. For a cost input, check that the page states the number for the setting given; whether it applies to this plan is not yours to judge. When the page states a different number for a num or rate item, give it as page_value. Decide only from the pages you fetch and the text below; do not read files. Return one status per item, under its ref: SUPPORTED, PARTIAL, UNSUPPORTED, CONTRADICTED or UNREACHABLE, with the page sentence you relied on.\nItems, one per line:\n{\\\"ref\\\":\\\"card:question\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Does widening a graph ingredient-substitution ranker raise its Hit@1 on Recipe1MSubs, once the 20.56 vs 34.53 baseline gap between two GISMo protocols is explained?\\\",\\\"sources\\\":[]}\n{\\\"ref\\\":\\\"card:hypothesis\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Hit@1 saturates by width 300 because GISMo already ranks 6,653 ingredients with a small GNN; more width won't help [s1].\\\",\\\"sources\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"s1\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://arxiv.org/html/2302.07960v1\\\",\\\"quote\\\":\\\"GISMo (Ours) 31.51±0.10 20.56±0.14 35.89±0.16 54.27±0.19\\\"}]}\n{\\\"ref\\\":\\\"card:if_lever\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Hit@1 climbs with width, at least +1 point from 300 to 512, showing ranker capacity is the lever.\\\",\\\"sources\\\":[]}\n{\\\"ref\\\":\\\"card:if_not\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Hit@1 is flat from 300 to 512 (within seed noise), so added width does not improve substitution ranking.\\\",\\\"sources\\\":[]}\n{\\\"ref\\\":\\\"card:test_summary\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Run Meta's official GISMo and Rita et al.'s protocol in one harness to reproduce 20.56 and 34.53, isolate the difference; then sweep width 64-512 at 5 seeds under the reproducing protocol and report both.\\\",\\\"sources\\\":[]}\n{\\\"ref\\\":\\\"card:closest_prior\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Meta's GISMo paper tuned width over 200-600 and kept 300, the largest width on this axis, but reported no width trend [s1].\\\",\\\"sources\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"s6\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://arxiv.org/html/2302.07960v1\\\",\\\"quote\\\":\\\"and both the number of features F and ingredient embedding dimension d using the set {200,300,400,500,600}\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"s1\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://arxiv.org/html/2302.07960v1\\\",\\\"quote\\\":\\\"GISMo (Ours) 31.51±0.10 20.56±0.14 35.89±0.16 54.27±0.19\\\"}],\\\"value\\\":600}\n{\\\"ref\\\":\\\"card:left_open\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"No published result reports how Hit@1 changes with ranker width 64-512 on Recipe1MSubs, under either protocol.\\\",\\\"sources\\\":[]}\n{\\\"ref\\\":\\\"card:anchor\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Reproduce Meta's Hit@1 20.56±0.14 [s1] with official code and data; independent 20.4 [s11].\\\",\\\"sources\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"s1\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://arxiv.org/html/2302.07960v1\\\",\\\"quote\\\":\\\"GISMo (Ours) 31.51±0.10 20.56±0.14 35.89±0.16 54.27±0.19\\\"},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"s11\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://ceur-ws.org/Vol-4196/paper_20.pdf\\\",\\\"quote\\\":\\\"Hits@1 20.4 20.3 20.6 20.6\\\"}],\\\"value\\\":20.56}\n{\\\"ref\\\":\\\"card:limits\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Shows general substitution Hit@1, not sustainability-specific substitutes; Recipe1MSubs is unlabeled for sustainability, so 'sustainable replacements' is only indirectly tested.\\\",\\\"sources\\\":[]}\n{\\\"ref\\\":\\\"src:s1\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://arxiv.org/html/2302.07960v1\\\",\\\"quote\\\":\\\"GISMo (Ours) 31.51±0.10 20.56±0.14 35.89±0.16 54.27±0.19\\\",\\\"supports\\\":\\\"meta_hit1=20.56, meta_hit1_std=0.14\\\"}\n{\\\"ref\\\":\\\"src:s11\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://ceur-ws.org/Vol-4196/paper_20.pdf\\\",\\\"quote\\\":\\\"Hits@1 20.4 20.3 20.6 20.6\\\",\\\"supports\\\":\\\"ceur_hit1=20.4 independent GISMo reproduction\\\"}\n{\\\"ref\\\":\\\"src:s6\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://arxiv.org/html/2302.07960v1\\\",\\\"quote\\\":\\\"and both the number of features F and ingredient embedding dimension d using the set {200,300,400,500,600}\\\",\\\"supports\\\":\\\"prior width tuning 200-600; novelty.prior_max_level=600\\\"}\n{\\\"ref\\\":\\\"num:vocab_size\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"ingredient vocabulary size\\\",\\\"value\\\":6653,\\\"unit\\\":\\\"ingredients\\\",\\\"basis\\\":\\\"CITED\\\",\\\"quote\\\":\\\"As a result, our ingredient vocabulary contains 6,653 ingredients.\\\",\\\"page_setting\\\":\\\"Recipe1M + Recipe1MSubs mapped to FlavorGraph\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://arxiv.org/html/2302.07960v1\\\"}\n{\\\"ref\\\":\\\"num:n_test\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"test substitution samples\\\",\\\"value\\\":10747,\\\"unit\\\":\\\"samples\\\",\\\"basis\\\":\\\"CITED\\\",\\\"quote\\\":\\\"Using the recipe IDs and following the Recipe1M dataset ID splits, we get 49,044, 10,729 and 10,747 substitution samples for training, validation, and test sets respectively.\\\",\\\"page_setting\\\":\\\"Recipe1MSubs\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://arxiv.org/html/2302.07960v1\\\"}\n{\\\"ref\\\":\\\"num:n_seeds\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"seeds per setting\\\",\\\"value\\\":5,\\\"unit\\\":\\\"runs\\\",\\\"basis\\\":\\\"CITED\\\",\\\"quote\\\":\\\"Results are averaged over 5 runs, and the mean ± std are reported.\\\",\\\"page_setting\\\":\\\"all GISMo results\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://arxiv.org/html/2302.07960v1\\\"}\n\nReturn only one JSON value, with no other text, that matches this JSON Schema:\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"object\\\",\\\"properties\\\":{\\\"items\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"array\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"One entry per item sent, with its ref unchanged.\\\",\\\"items\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"object\\\",\\\"properties\\\":{\\\"ref\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"string\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"\\\\\"card:<field>\\\\\", \\\\\"src:<source id>\\\\\", \\\\\"num